This machine's lasting kernel settings.

Each file here whose name ends in .conf holds settings, one a line:

    net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1

At every boot (and at "sudo netlab restart") the files are read in name
order, so 90-forward.conf comes after 10-defaults.conf, and when two files
set the same key, the later one wins. A setting made live with sysctl -w
lasts only until then.

Only network settings, whose keys start with net., belong to a machine:
anything else is left out, with a line in "journalctl -u netlab".
